A large '''droid army''' under the command of a the [[T-series military strategic analysis and tactics droid|T-series tactical droid]] [[TN-123]] and was deployed to [[Malastare]] during the [[Clone Wars]] in the [[Standard year|year]] [[21 BBY]] to secure the [[planet]]'s [[Malastarian fuel|fuel]] deposits for the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]]. The ensuing [[Battle of Malastare|battle]] was one of the longest and fiercest of the conflict, with the [[droid]]s nearly capturing Malastare from the [[Galactic Republic]]. On the verge of defeat, the [[Grand Army of the Republic]] deployed an experimental [[electro-proton bomb]] that disabled the entire droid [[army]] in one fell swoop, inadvertently unearthing a [[Zillo Beast]] that dwelt beneath the battlefield.

==Characteristics==
The [[droid]] [[army]] incorporated several different models of [[battle droid]]s that were used by the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] [[Confederacy military|military forces]], such as [[B1-series battle droid]]s, [[B2-series super battle droid]]s, [[DSD1 dwarf spider droid]]s, [[LM-432 crab droid]]s, [[LR-57 combat/retail droid]]s, [[NR-N99 Persuader-class droid enforcer|NR-N99 ''Persuader''-class droid enforcers]], [[Hyena-class Droid Fighter/Bomber|''Hyena''-class Droid Bombers]], and [[Vulture-class starfighter|Vulture droid starfighters]]. Several [[Armored Assault Tank Mk I|Armored Assault Tanks]] were also used by the army.<ref name="The Zillo Beast" />

The army's NR-N99 [[Droid tank|tank droids]] used minimal tread so as to avoid kicking up dust that might blind their fellow [[droid]] [[soldier]]s.<ref name="Build R2-D2 34">{{BuildR2Cite|34|Droid Directory}}</ref>

==History==
[[File:SWBook-BattleDroidsMarch.png|thumb|left|350px|A grouping of the army's B1 battle droids]]
During the [[Battle of Malastare]] of the [[Clone Wars]]<ref name="The Zillo Beast" /> in [[21 BBY]],<ref name="Date" /> the [[Separatist Droid Army]] deployed a large army of battle droids to the [[planet]] [[Malastare]], commanded by<ref name="The Zillo Beast" /> [[TN-123]]<ref name="Battles">''[[Star Wars: Battles that Changed the Galaxy]]''</ref> to secure the planet's [[Malastarian fuel|fuel]] deposits for use by the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]].<ref name="New Edition">''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]''</ref> One of the longest and most fierce battles of the war, [[Grand Army of the Republic|the Grand Army]] of the [[Galactic Republic]] deployed an experimental [[electro-proton bomb]] that was powerful enough to disable the entire droid army in one fell swoop, which inadvertently formed a [[sinkhole]], revealing a [[Zillo Beast]] that dwelt beneath the planet's surface.<ref name="The Zillo Beast" />

==Behind the scenes==
The droid army first appeared in "[[The Zillo Beast]],"<ref name="The Zillo Beast" /> the eighteenth episode of the animated television series ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' [[The Clone Wars: Season Two|second season]], which aired on [[April 9]], [[2010]].<ref name="EpGuide">{{SWArchive|url=theclonewars/guide/episode218.html|text=''The Clone Wars'' Episode Guide: The Zillo Beast}}</ref>

